Subject: [PATCH] core: Fire Emblem Fates helpers: New Game defaults writer

Round 81 (docs/ROUND81_PLAN.md A2, build/r81/hook/HOOK_TRACE.md; the owner's
pick F-057 #5 and its new writer group, answered "ok keep going", run on the
standing OK F-059 (3)). Stores the Esc window's four New Game rows (patch
0039) into the game's Options block once per New Game, as if they had been
set on the game's own Options screen before the Prologue.

New core fates_options.rs, on the patch 0031 / 0035 trap machinery:
- The trap: while the title is Fire Emblem Fates (is_fates_title(), so Seal
  of Flames too) and at least one New Game row is not Game's choice, the
  first word of GameConfigData::StartFromBeginning 0x001D0618 (original
  0xE92D4070) becomes the reserved svc 0xEFFEC003 (0xEFFEC001 chests,
  0xEFFEC002 names); the recompiled code is checked again. Every row back at
  Game's choice, or a save state that brought the svc back with the rows off:
  the original word goes back at the frame's end. A stranger word is left
  alone (one log line); recompiled code that cannot check itself keeps the
  trap off (one log line).
- At the svc (kernel/svc.rs dispatch): only checks, then "pending": ARM at
  0x001D0618, lr == 0x00441794 (the one call, in JumpMyUnitEdit), r0 ==
  *G_GameConfig (0x006DA0F8) and not 0, +0x4..+0x18 readable, no player army
  (fates_nuzlocke::in_game, the randomizer's test), no map (Map::Get's global
  *0x006D72F4 readable and 0). The replaced push {r4-r6, lr} is done whatever
  the checks say; no guest data byte is written inside the svc.
- At the end of that frame (System::run_frame, right after
  fates_rando_session::after_frame and outside its randomizer gate, so
  NewGameWatch still sees the block unchanged in the pick frame): the checks
  again on the recorded block, then each set row's byte stored only if it
  differs: +0x8 battle animations, +0xC map speed, +0xD enemy turn skip,
  +0x16 HP bars. Never word +0x4, never +0xE, never the versus copy, no game
  function call. An offset outside the four or a value at or past its line's
  size refuses the whole write. One log line, "fates_options: New Game:
  battle 1->0, speed 2->1, ..." (bytes before and after).
- Defaults are today's game: with every row at Game's choice no word is laid
  and the writer reads no guest memory, except one read of the trap word
  after a frame that does not follow the one before (a save state loaded, or
  the writer starting late), so a state taken with the svc is put right.

Desk trace before the code (build/r81/writer/JUMP4.md): MainSequence::Jump(4)
lands on label 4 (GameElapse::Create, title::MyUnitEdit::Create); the
creator's Regist jumps to label 7 (chapter-save steps, then the castle and
chapter labels 5 and 6). No GameConfigData::Reset between StartFromBeginning
and the Prologue: GameReset sits only in labels 2 and 3 (title, main menu),
reached only by backing out of the creator, after which a new pick writes
again. The write point stays at the pick frame's end.

lib.rs: the module, a System field `options` (fates_options::Writer), the one
run_frame call line, and the set_helpers log line also names the four rows.

Tests (13, fates_options): the word rule and a stranger word; the replaced
push; every svc refusal with a planted bug (Thumb, wrong place, wrong lr,
wrong r0 = the versus copy, null r0, G_GameConfig null, block unreadable,
player army, map, Map::Get's global unreadable); the store writes exactly
+0x8 / +0xC / +0xD / +0x16 and compares first (never +0x4 or +0xE, the
versus copy untouched); every frame's-end refusal writes nothing; a value
past its line or another offset refuses the whole write; all rows Game's
choice lays no word and touches no guest memory over 199 frames; a set row
lays the word and Game's choice puts it back; a state with the word is put
right with the rows off (and drops a pending store); a state with the
original word gets the trap again; NewGameWatch still fires in the pick frame
